WEBVTT

NOTE Cues sit near the top (line:4%) so they don't cover on-screen labels.

1a-1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.607 line:4% align:center
MOSAIC’s question bank is built from

1a-2
00:00:02.607 --> 00:00:05.300 line:4% align:center
requirements and guidance in source documents.

1b-1
00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:07.230 line:4% align:center
Let’s follow one.

2a-1
00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:11.393 line:4% align:center
This question comes from the CDP questionnaire

2a-2
00:00:11.393 --> 00:00:13.720 line:4% align:center
for small and medium enterprises:

2b-1
00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:16.785 line:4% align:center
Does your organization have an environmental

2b-2
00:00:16.785 --> 00:00:19.400 line:4% align:center
policy that addresses environmental issues?

2c-1
00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.757 line:4% align:center
This question, together with its follow-up

2c-2
00:00:22.757 --> 00:00:25.316 line:4% align:center
options and guidance, identifies several

2c-3
00:00:25.316 --> 00:00:26.340 line:4% align:center
distinct things:

3a-1
00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:29.871 line:4% align:center
whether a policy exists, and whether it covers

3a-2
00:00:29.871 --> 00:00:32.664 line:4% align:center
the company’s operations, suppliers, and

3a-3
00:00:32.664 --> 00:00:34.200 line:4% align:center
downstream activities.

3b-1
00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:37.463 line:4% align:center
Each one is recorded as an atomic indicator,

3b-2
00:00:37.463 --> 00:00:39.690 line:4% align:center
small enough to answer on its own.

3c-1
00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.140 line:4% align:center
Each keeps a source reference and a supporting excerpt.

4a-1
00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:46.560 line:4% align:center
Then the same idea is looked for across the

4a-2
00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:47.820 line:4% align:center
whole knowledge base.

4b-1
00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:50.992 line:4% align:center
Related requirements about policies, targets and

4b-2
00:00:50.992 --> 00:00:53.830 line:4% align:center
tracking are grouped together: twenty-three of

4b-3
00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:57.100 line:4% align:center
them, from eleven of the forty-four source documents.

4c-1
00:00:57.330 --> 00:01:00.352 line:4% align:center
Grouping means a business isn’t asked the same

4c-2
00:01:00.352 --> 00:01:02.980 line:4% align:center
thing over and over, in different words.

5a-1
00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:06.030 line:4% align:center
That recurrence sets the base weight.

5b-1
00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:09.455 line:4% align:center
The weighting combines two signals: how widely

5b-2
00:01:09.455 --> 00:01:12.321 line:4% align:center
the theme appears across documents, and how

5b-3
00:01:12.321 --> 00:01:14.320 line:4% align:center
frequently it appears overall.

5c-1
00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:17.282 line:4% align:center
Their relative ranks receive seventy-five and

5c-2
00:01:17.282 --> 00:01:19.674 line:4% align:center
twenty-five percent respectively, then are

5c-3
00:01:19.674 --> 00:01:21.040 line:4% align:center
scaled from one to five.

5d-1
00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:24.810 line:4% align:center
Here, that gives three point eight six out of five.

6a-1
00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:27.590 line:4% align:center
The group becomes plain questions.

6b-1
00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:30.761 line:4% align:center
Does your company have a written environmental

6b-2
00:01:30.761 --> 00:01:33.735 line:4% align:center
policy that applies to your own operations? And

6b-3
00:01:33.735 --> 00:01:36.520 line:4% align:center
does it also cover suppliers, and customers?

6c-1
00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:40.189 line:4% align:center
Each one gets an answer scale, a category, and a

6c-2
00:01:40.189 --> 00:01:43.320 line:4% align:center
rule for who is asked. This one goes to every

6c-3
00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:44.990 line:4% align:center
business, of every size.

7a-1
00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:48.647 line:4% align:center
All of this is stored as configuration: readable

7a-2
00:01:48.647 --> 00:01:51.200 line:4% align:center
settings the app uses in every assessment.

7b-1
00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:53.776 line:4% align:center
Change the documents, and the questions and

7b-2
00:01:53.776 --> 00:01:55.770 line:4% align:center
weights could be rebuilt the same way.

8a-1
00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:59.100 line:4% align:center
MOSAIC. The pieces that matter.
